From: sheng-development
Subject: [PATCH] Start polling for claims made while discovery was still running

The hotplug path in sensor_changes() already handles a sensor appearing
under existing claimants -- it checks g_hash_table_size(ht) and calls
driver_set_polling(). The initial find_sensors() path has no such check,
because upstream nothing can claim before it finishes.

The SSC discovery wait is ~20s, and KWin claims the accelerometer as soon
as the bus name registers, so on sheng it always lands inside that window.
The claim is accepted and recorded in data->clients[], the sensor is opened
seconds later, and nothing ever starts it: Claim() returned success, KWin
believes it is subscribed, and no reading ever arrives. Auto-rotate stays
dead until something re-runs KWin's applySensorChanges -- toggling the
policy in System Settings, a lid event, or a tablet-mode change.

Start polling for any sensor that already has clients once discovery is
done.
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -787,6 +787,14 @@
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
 		goto bail;
 
+	/* A client can claim during the SSC discovery wait, and unlike the
+	 * hotplug path nothing here would ever start polling for it. */
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
+		if (driver_type_exists (data, i) &&
+		    g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0)
+			driver_set_polling (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i), TRUE);
+	}
+
 	/* Clients that read the properties during the SSC discovery wait saw
 	 * every sensor as absent, and no claim means no directed signal. */
 	send_dbus_event_for_client (data, NULL, PROP_ALL);
